PROSE:
The polished marble of the sanctum entrance offered no cover, leaving the party entirely exposed as the heavy doors loomed ahead. Vance didn't hesitate; he slammed his Rebar against the stone stairs, the harsh metallic ringing instantly drawing the aggro of the two towering elite guards stationed at the threshold. The gilded constructs pivoted, their optical sensors locking onto him as his status window flickered, confirming he was holding the line on a mere 10 HP. That desperate gambit gave Rhea the exact opening she needed, her fingers tightening around the heavy, light-swallowing mass of the Null-Value Token as she sprinted past the distracted sentinels toward the locked gates.

[Aggro Target Acquired: Vance Harrow]

The guards moved with terrifying, bureaucratic efficiency. One swung a massive stamp-hammer, the brass head glowing with administrative force. Vance raised his Rebar, catching the blow on a desperate angle. The impact drove him to his knees, the shockwave rattling his teeth, but the makeshift weapon held. 

[Damage Mitigated. HP: 6/100.]

Rhea reached the heavy sanctum doors. The locking mechanism was a complex array of shifting gears and glowing runes, demanding proper clearance codes and a substantial mana tariff. She didn't have either. What she had was a physical divide-by-zero error. 

She slammed the Null-Value Token directly into the center of the locking mechanism. 

[System Error: Invalid Input. Value = NULL.]
[Calculating... Calculating... Fatal Exception.]

The heavy metal doors shrieked as a localized physics glitch rippled outward. The stone around the frame warped, colors inverting for a split second before the entire entrance shattered inward in a shower of twisted iron and corrupted code. 

Rhea didn't wait for the dust to settle. She surged into the Sanctum Foyer, her boots crunching over the ruined doors. Behind her, Vance roared, using the momentum of the guards' missed strikes against them. A red-tape tether lashed out from the second construct's wrist, wrapping around Vance's ankle, but he twisted, bringing the Rebar down in a brutal arc that shattered the construct's knee joint.

"Inside!" Rhea yelled. 

Vance threw his weight forward, dragging the crippled guard with him as he crossed the threshold. The first guard followed, its stamp-hammer raised for a lethal strike. Rhea grabbed a jagged piece of the shattered door frame and drove it into the exposed, sparking wiring of the construct's neck joint just as Vance swept its legs. The gilded construct crashed onto the marble floor of the foyer, its optical sensors flickering out as Vance brought his Rebar down on its cranial casing to finish it. 

[Elite Bureaucratic Guard Defeated. XP Awarded.]
[Elite Bureaucratic Guard Defeated. XP Awarded.]

Vance collapsed against the wall, clutching his ribs where the stamp-hammer had grazed him. He coughed, a wet, rattling sound, as the heavy doors behind them began to hiss, sealing them inside the foyer.

[Status Effect: Heavy Blunt-Force Trauma applied.]
[HP: 2/100.]

"Don't die on me yet," Rhea said, her chest heaving as she stared at his blinking health bar.

"Just... doing the math," Vance wheezed, wiping a smear of blood from his chin. "Two hit points is still alive."

